Turen Java Inspect is a bounded offline Java .class/.jar static-inspection
WebAssembly module. It is the JVM counterpart to the monodis (.NET CIL)
target.

The class-file parser, bytecode disassembler, findings scanner, and JAR
walker are original Turen code implementing the public JVMS class-file
format specification. No javap/JDK code is included.

It directly uses one permissively licensed crate:

- zip 9.0.5 (https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2), MIT, for
  read-only JAR/ZIP central-directory listing and bounded per-entry inflate
  via flate2 and the pure-Rust zlib-rs 0.6.7 backend (Zlib license).
  No archive extraction or
  path APIs are used.

The compiled module also embeds other permissively licensed crates.io
dependencies (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, Unicode, or Zlib licensed; see
Cargo.lock for the full closure) and Rust standard-library components
distributed under Apache-2.0 or MIT.

Turen added the bounded WebAssembly wrapper, the findings and degradation
surfaces, and the packaging.

